-- allium: 3

-- Module: reconcile.
-- Scope: the per-pod loop. A poll outcome becomes a pod state (the §5 state
-- diagram), the desired annotation state is compared with the last applied
-- state, a patch happens only on meaningful change, a throttled change stays
-- pending, no patch is made once deletionTimestamp is set (§4), and a
-- Deployment rollout gets no special handling (§8 failure modes, §9.13).
-- Owner: ticket 21 for the unknown and unreachable policy (§9.6). The decided
-- loop safeguards, including the rollout rule, are built by the round-2
-- spec-then-build ticket 31; the rollout guidance page is ticket 34.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "§9.6 Transient failure: how many polls and how much time the last-known value is kept after a timeout, 5xx or unparsable payload before knarr removes the annotation, the neutral value cost_mapping's Absent fixes (§5)."
open question "§9.6 Absent contract: how many consecutive 404 or refused polls since the pod started mark the contract absent, and whether a NetworkPolicy block is distinguishable from it (§8 failure modes)."
open question "§9.6 Unmanaged: what knarr does on an absent contract: remove the annotations it owns, emit a per-Deployment Event and metric, and whether it keeps polling."
open question "§9.6 Just started: how long a pod stays unannotated before its first valid poll, and whether pods without a pod IP are tracked at all (§5; every pod with a pod IP is polled whatever its phase or readiness, see worker_contract Discovery)."
